{"qid":"Q680472","names":["Principality of Volhynia"],"title":"Principality of Volhynia","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Principality of Volhynia was a western Kievan Rus' polity centered on the fortress city of Volodymyr (modern Volodymyr, Ukraine), established under Rurikid princes in the late tenth century. Its most consequential ruler, Roman the Great (r. 1170–1205), unified Volhynia and expanded its reach, then in 1199 annexed the neighboring Principality of Halych after its ruling line died out, forging the Kingdom of Galicia-Volhynia. Roman pursued an aggressive western policy, clashing with Poland and Lithuania, and was killed in battle near Zawichost in 1205.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The principality's heartland around Volodymyr is well-attested in chronicles; exact boundaries fluctuated with sub-appanages and are incompletely mapped for the eleventh century.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Principality of Volhynia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principality_of_Volhynia"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Roman the Great","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_the_Great"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Kingdom of Galicia–Volhynia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Galicia%E2%80%93Volhynia"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Principality of Volhynia","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Igor Yaroslavich","nativeName":"Ігор Ярославич","roman":"Igor Yaroslavich","start":1056,"end":1057,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Rostislav Vladimirovich","nativeName":"Ростислав Володимирович","roman":"Rostislav Vladimirovich","start":1057,"end"